{"name":"Soft Violet","hex":"#e9e6e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily giving way under pressure.","Smooth and flexible; not rough, rugged, or harsh."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Be quiet; hold; stop; not so fast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft"},{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Violet (Peanuts)","blocks":[{"text":"Violet Gray is a fictional character featured in the long-running syndicated daily and Sunday comic strip Peanuts, created by Charles M. Schulz. Violet first appeared in the February 7, 1951 strip. She was originally a major character, until she was eventually relegated to background and cameo appearances as other female characters became more prominent, with Lucy ultimately taking over most of Violet's character traits. Violet is a snob who likes bragging and, along with her best friends Lucy and Patty, often teases and torments Charlie Brown; however, she is generally softer in this regard than Lucy. She bullies other characters in the strip, particularly \"Pig-Pen\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/VioletGray.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_(Peanuts)","wikidata":"Q1084304"},{"title":"Violet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is the color of light at the short wavelength end of the visible spectrum. It is one of the seven colors that Isaac Newton labeled when dividing the spectrum of visible light in 1704. Violet light has a wavelength between approximately 380 and 435 nanometers. The color's name is derived from the Viola genus of flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Amatista_Laye_2.jpg/330px-Amatista_Laye_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_(color)","wikidata":"Q428124"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Chasublepurple.jpg/330px-Chasublepurple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Chasublepurple.jpg/330px-Chasublepurple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChasublepurple.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Manganese_violet.jpg/330px-Manganese_violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Manganese_violet.jpg/330px-Manganese_violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManganese_violet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg/500px-Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg/1280px-Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg/500px-Sweet_Violet_%28Viola_odorata%29_-_London%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut